doc:sec-272-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "272(5) Core terms of workplace determinations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The determination must not include a term that would, if the determination were an enterprise agreement, mean that the FWC could not approve the agreement:  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-273 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "273 Mandatory terms of workplace determinations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-273 ;
    values:originalText "Mandatory terms (1) This section sets out the mandatory terms that a workplace determination must include. Term about settling disputes (2) The determination must include a term that provides a procedure for settling disputes: (a) about any matters arising under the determination; and (b) in relation to the National Employment Standards. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to the determination if the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination would, if the determination were an enterprise agreement, satisfy paragraphs 186(6)(a) and (b) (which deal with terms in enterprise agreements about settling disputes). Flexibility term (4) The determination must include the model flexibility term unless the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination would, if the determination were an enterprise agreement, satisfy paragraph 202(1)(a) and section 203 (which deal with flexibility terms in enterprise agreements). Consultation term (5) The determination must include the model consultation term unless the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Workplace determinations  Part 2-5 Core terms, mandatory terms and agreed terms of workplace determinations etc." ;
    skos:definition "Mandatory terms (1) This section sets out the mandatory terms that a workplace determination must include. Term about settling disputes (2) The determination must include a term that provides a procedure for settling disputes: (a) about any matters arising under the determination; and (b) in relation to the National Employment Standards. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to the determination if the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination would, if the determination were an enterprise agreement, satisfy paragraphs 186(6)(a) and (b) (which deal with terms in enterprise agreements about settling disputes). Flexibility term (4) The determination must include the model flexibility term unless the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination would, if the determination were an enterprise agreement, satisfy paragraph 202(1)(a) and section 203 (which deal with flexibility terms in enterprise agreements). Consultation term (5) The determination must include the model consultation term unless the FWC is satisfied that an agreed term for the determination  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Workplace determinations  Part 2-5 Core terms, mandatory terms and agreed terms of workplace determinations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5a08285cf7776a925b53efac97073fef975523ff0dc086800f96f9fc0778358d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
