doc:sec-296-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "296(1) Variation of national minimum wage order to remove ambiguity" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A determination varying a national minimum wage order under section 296 comes into operation on the day specified in the determination. Note: For when a national minimum wage order comes into operation, see section 287.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "61"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-298 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "298 Special rule about retrospective variations of national minimum"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-298 ;
    values:originalText "wage orders Application of this section (1) This section applies if a determination varying a national minimum wage order has a retrospective effect because it comes into operation under subsection 297(2) on a day before the day on which the determination is made. No creation of liability to pay pecuniary penalty for past conduct (2) If: (a) a person engaged in conduct before the determination was made; and (b) but for the retrospective effect of the determination, the conduct would not have contravened a term of the national minimum wage order or an enterprise agreement; a court must not order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to the conduct, on the grounds that the conduct contravened a term of the national minimum wage order or enterprise agreement. Note 1: This subsection does not affect the powers of a court to make other kinds of orders under Division 2 of Part 4-1. Note 2: A determination varying a national minimum wage order could result in a contravention of a term of an enterprise agreement because of the effect of subsection 206(4).  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Minimum wages  Part 2-6 National minimum wage orders  Division 4 Section 299 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 299  When a national minimum wage order is in operation A national minimum wage order continues in operation until the next national minimum wage order comes into operation. Note: For when a national minimum wage order comes into operation, see section 287.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "wage orders Application of this section (1) This section applies if a determination varying a national minimum wage order has a retrospective effect because it comes into operation under subsection 297(2) on a day before the day on which the determination is made. No creation of liability to pay pecuniary penalty for past conduct (2) If: (a) a person engaged in conduct before the determination was made; and (b) but for the retrospective effect of the determination, the conduct would not have contravened a term of the national minimum wage order or an enterprise agreement; a court must not order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to the conduct, on the grounds that the conduct contravened a term of the national minimum wage order or enterprise agreement. Note 1: This subsection does not affect the powers of a court to make other kinds of orders under Division 2 of Part 4-1. Note 2: A determination varying a national minimum wage order could result in a contravention of a term of an enterprise agreement because of the effect of subsection 206(4).  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Minimum wages  Part 2-6 National minimum wage orders  Division 4 Section 299 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 299  When a national minimum wage order is in operation A national minimum wage order continues in operation until the next national minimum wage order comes into operation. Note: For when a national minimum wage order comes into operation, see section 287.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ef06b7d1858a6a8a0d1eadd593b43f3ca231065e2c665e19d5ec573adab782b3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
