doc:sec-306ea a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "306EA Regulated labour hire arrangement order may cover" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "additional arrangements Determination that application covers additional employers and employees (1) If an application for a regulated labour hire arrangement order is made in relation to a regulated host, an employer and one or more employees of the employer, the FWC may determine that the application is taken to also relate to: (a) one or more other employers (each of which is an additional employer) that the FWC is satisfied supply or will supply, in the manner referred to in paragraph 306E(1)(a), one or more employees to perform work, for the regulated host, of the kind in relation to which the application was made; and (b) the employees referred to in paragraph (a) of this subsection (each of whom is an additional regulated employee).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "75"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306eb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "306EB Application of regulated labour hire arrangement order to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-306eb ;
    values:originalText "new covered employment instrument (1) This section applies if: (a) a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force; and (b) the host employment instrument covered by the order ceases to apply to the regulated host covered by the order, or to a class of employees of the regulated host covered by the order, in connection with another covered employment instrument (the new instrument) starting to apply to the regulated host or those employees; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "new covered employment instrument (1) This section applies if: (a) a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force; and (b) the host employment instrument covered by the order ceases to apply to the regulated host covered by the order, or to a class of employees of the regulated host covered by the order, in connection with another covered employment instrument (the new instrument) starting to apply to the regulated host or those employees; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
