concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306m a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "306M Making an alternative protected rate of pay order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-306m ;
    values:originalText "Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (b) a regulated labour hire arrangement order has been made but is not yet in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (c) an application for a regulated labour hire arrangement order that would cover a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host has been made to the FWC under section 306E but has not been finally determined. Alternative protected rate of pay order (2) The FWC may make an order (an alternative protected rate of pay order) specifying:  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (b) a regulated labour hire arrangement order has been made but is not yet in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (c) an application for a regulated labour hire arrangement order that would cover a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host has been made to the FWC under section 306E but has not been finally determined. Alternative protected rate of pay order (2) The FWC may make an order (an alternative protected rate of pay order) specifying:  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0ccdf42586937399ceba0f448d92994a11335c8f0a2c4f649309a780bb974a92" ;
    cof:pageNumber "91"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306m-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306m-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.91" .
doc:sec-306m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "306M Making an alternative protected rate of pay order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (b) a regulated labour hire arrangement order has been made but is not yet in force that covers a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host; or (c) an application for a regulated labour hire arrangement order that would cover a regulated host, an employer and a regulated employee of the employer performing work for the regulated host has been made to the FWC under section 306E but has not been finally determined. Alternative protected rate of pay order (2) The FWC may make an order (an alternative protected rate of pay order) specifying:  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "91"^^xsd:integer .

