concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "306Q Dealing with disputes by arbitration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-306q ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may deal with the dispute by arbitration, including by making an order (an arbitrated protected rate of pay order) determining: (a) how the rate of pay at which the employer must pay the employee in connection with the work is to be worked out; and (b) that the employer must pay the rate of pay worked out in that way to the employee in connection with the work.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC may deal with the dispute by arbitration, including by making an order (an arbitrated protected rate of pay order) determining: (a) how the rate of pay at which the employer must pay the employee in connection with the work is to be worked out; and (b) that the employer must pay the rate of pay worked out in that way to the employee in connection with the work.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "85bbc17897490047a1ce0523e92978b92cea4034393a30b91e52656de16a1083" ;
    cof:pageNumber "99"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must pay employee a certain rate of pay." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.99" ;
