doc:sec-306u a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "306U Short-term arrangements—entering into other labour hire" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "agreements A regulated host covered by a regulated labour hire arrangement order contravenes this section if: (a) an employer covered by the regulated labour hire arrangement order is not required to pay a regulated employee at a rate determined under or in accordance with this Part because of the operation of subsection 306G(2) (including as it applies because of subsection 306M(9) or 306Q(8)); and (b) the regulated host enters into an agreement that has the result that another person is to perform the same, or substantially the same, work as that performed by the regulated employee for the regulated host; and (c) it could reasonably be concluded that the purpose, or one of the purposes, of engaging the other person is to achieve the result that the employer is not required to pay a regulated employee at a rate determined under or in accordance with this Part. Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-306v a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "306V Engaging independent contractors"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-306v ;
    values:originalText "An employer covered by a regulated labour hire arrangement order contravenes this section if: (a) the employer dismisses an employee who performs, or is to perform, work for a regulated host covered by the order; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Regulated labour hire arrangement orders  Part 2-7A Anti-avoidance  Division 4 Section 306V Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) the employer engages another person as an independent contractor, under a contract for services, to perform that work, or work of that kind, for the regulated host; and (c) a result of the employer dismissing the employee and engaging the independent contractor is that the employer is not required to pay a person at a rate determined under or in accordance with this Part; and (d) it could reasonably be concluded that the employer dismissed the employee and engaged the independent contractor for the purpose, or purposes including the purpose, of achieving that result. Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "An employer covered by a regulated labour hire arrangement order contravenes this section if: (a) the employer dismisses an employee who performs, or is to perform, work for a regulated host covered by the order; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Regulated labour hire arrangement orders  Part 2-7A Anti-avoidance  Division 4 Section 306V Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) the employer engages another person as an independent contractor, under a contract for services, to perform that work, or work of that kind, for the regulated host; and (c) a result of the employer dismissing the employee and engaging the independent contractor is that the employer is not required to pay a person at a rate determined under or in accordance with this Part; and (d) it could reasonably be concluded that the employer dismissed the employee and engaged the independent contractor for the purpose, or purposes including the purpose, of achieving that result. Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fe9e89dd59d3928878dd745a7093f44208740bd4b3d2cdeb442450519582101e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must not dismiss employee and engage independent contractor to avoid paying a worker." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
