doc:sec-313 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "313 Transferring employees and new employer covered by" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "transferable instrument (1) If a transferable instrument covered the old employer and a transferring employee immediately before the termination of the transferring employee’s employment with the old employer, then: (a) the transferable instrument covers the new employer and the transferring employee in relation to the transferring work after the time (the transfer time) the transferring employee becomes employed by the new employer; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-314 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "314 New non-transferring employees of new employer may be"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-314 ;
    values:originalText "covered by transferable instrument (1) If: (a) a transferable instrument covers the new employer because of paragraph 313(1)(a); and (b) after the transferable instrument starts to cover the new employer, the new employer employs a non-transferring employee; and (c) the non-transferring employee performs the transferring work; and (d) at the time the non-transferring employee is employed, no other enterprise agreement or modern award covers the new employer and the non-transferring employee in relation to that work; then the transferable instrument covers the new employer and the non-transferring employee in relation to that work. (2) A non-transferring employee of a new employer, in relation to a transfer of business, is an employee of the new employer who is not a transferring employee.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Transfer of business  Part 2-8 Transfer of instruments  Division 2 Section 315 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (3) This section has effect subject to any FWC order under subsection 319(1)." ;
    skos:definition "covered by transferable instrument (1) If: (a) a transferable instrument covers the new employer because of paragraph 313(1)(a); and (b) after the transferable instrument starts to cover the new employer, the new employer employs a non-transferring employee; and (c) the non-transferring employee performs the transferring work; and (d) at the time the non-transferring employee is employed, no other enterprise agreement or modern award covers the new employer and the non-transferring employee in relation to that work; then the transferable instrument covers the new employer and the non-transferring employee in relation to that work. (2) A non-transferring employee of a new employer, in relation to a transfer of business, is an employee of the new employer who is not a transferring employee.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Transfer of business  Part 2-8 Transfer of instruments  Division 2 Section 315 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (3) This section has effect subject to any FWC order under subsection 319(1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e164d00a20fa8e620910ba0cd0a6d782751dd7b55fece755d95bfb40d62e6bd9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
