concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-316-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "316(5) Transferring employees who are high income employees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-316-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If: (a) the transferring employee is entitled to non-monetary benefits under the guarantee of annual earnings after the transfer time; and (b) it is not practicable for the new employer to provide those benefits to the transferring employee; then the guarantee of annual earnings is taken to be varied so that, instead of the entitlement to those benefits, the transferring employee is entitled to an amount of money that is equivalent to the agreed money value of those benefits." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If: (a) the transferring employee is entitled to non-monetary benefits under the guarantee of annual earnings after the transfer time; and (b) it is not practicable for the new employer to provide those benefits to the transferring employee; then the guarantee of annual earnings is taken to be varied so that, instead of the entitlement to those benefits, the transferring employee is entitled to an amount of money that is equivalent to the agreed money value of those benefits."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "089269d30236160c112e1d763b3c0a98b18d6c031da97d35e330964d6b60af49" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-316 ;
    cof:pageNumber "114"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Guarantee of annual earnings must be varied if non-monetary benefits cannot be provided." ;
    dc:description "Amount of money equivalent to agreed benefits" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
