doc:sec-318-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "318(1) Orders relating to instruments covering new employer and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may make the following orders: (a) an order that a transferable instrument that would, or would be likely to, cover the new employer and a transferring employee because of paragraph 313(1)(a) does not, or will not, cover the new employer and the transferring employee; (b) an order that an enterprise agreement or a named employer award that covers the new employer covers, or will cover, the transferring employee. Who may apply for an order" ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-318-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "318(2) Orders relating to instruments covering new employer and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-318-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC may make the order only on application by any of the following: (a) the new employer or a person who is likely to be the new employer; (b) a transferring employee, or an employee who is likely to be a transferring employee; (c) if the application relates to an enterprise agreement—an employee organisation that is, or is likely to be, covered by the agreement; (d) if the application relates to a named employer award—an employee organisation that is entitled to represent the  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Transfer of business  Part 2-8 Powers of the FWC  Division 3 Section 318 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 industrial interests of an employee referred to in paragraph (b). Matters that the FWC must take into account" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The FWC may make the order only on application by any of the following: (a) the new employer or a person who is likely to be the new employer; (b) a transferring employee, or an employee who is likely to be a transferring employee; (c) if the application relates to an enterprise agreement—an employee organisation that is, or is likely to be, covered by the agreement; (d) if the application relates to a named employer award—an employee organisation that is entitled to represent the  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Transfer of business  Part 2-8 Powers of the FWC  Division 3 Section 318 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 industrial interests of an employee referred to in paragraph (b). Matters that the FWC must take into account"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5bb22679ae5653cfa58b7f065353f2dc2c9ad8d9f0cf5af54dadee3bf93a67b7" ;
