doc:sec-325-ss-1a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "325(1A) Unreasonable requirements to spend or pay amount" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1A) An employer (the prospective employer) must not directly or indirectly require another person (the prospective employee) to spend, or pay to the prospective employer or any other person, an amount of the prospective employee’s money if: (a) the requirement is in connection with employment or potential employment of the prospective employee by the prospective employer; and (b) the requirement is unreasonable in the circumstances; and (c) the payment is directly or indirectly for the benefit of the prospective employer or a party related to the prospective employer. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "126"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-325-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "325(2) Unreasonable requirements to spend or pay amount"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-325-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a requirement referred to in subsection (1) or (1A) is or is not reasonable.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Other terms and conditions of employment  Part 2-9 Payment of wages etc.  Division 2 Section 326 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a requirement referred to in subsection (1) or (1A) is or is not reasonable.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Other terms and conditions of employment  Part 2-9 Payment of wages etc.  Division 2 Section 326 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "117f8caa34609fe8776790b640b4ef458c6430236c9e245d3ace75e6f46e9b48" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-325 ;
    cof:pageNumber "126"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Circumstances in which a requirement is or is not reasonable" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
