    skos:definition "(1) A term of a modern award, an enterprise agreement or a contract of employment has no effect to the extent that the term permits, or has the effect of permitting, an employer to deduct an amount from an amount that is payable to an employee in relation to the performance of work, if the deduction is: (a) directly or indirectly for the benefit of the employer or a party related to the employer; and (b) unreasonable in the circumstances."@en ;
