concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "333 High income threshold"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-333 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this section, the high income threshold is the amount prescribed by, or worked out in the manner prescribed by, the regulations. (2) A regulation made for the purposes of subsection (1) has no effect to the extent that it would have the effect of reducing the amount of the high income threshold. (3) If: (a) in prescribing a manner in which the high income threshold is worked out, regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) specify a particular matter or state of affairs; and (b) as a result of a change in the matter or state of affairs, the amount of the high income threshold worked out in that manner would, but for this subsection, be less than it was on the last occasion on which this subsection did not apply;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to this section, the high income threshold is the amount prescribed by, or worked out in the manner prescribed by, the regulations. (2) A regulation made for the purposes of subsection (1) has no effect to the extent that it would have the effect of reducing the amount of the high income threshold. (3) If: (a) in prescribing a manner in which the high income threshold is worked out, regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) specify a particular matter or state of affairs; and (b) as a result of a change in the matter or state of affairs, the amount of the high income threshold worked out in that manner would, but for this subsection, be less than it was on the last occasion on which this subsection did not apply;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28c249edf0bb7e6d827a03e093f6e1ef122a82fa302354db6dabe240fc15eede" ;
    cof:pageNumber "137"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.137" .
doc:sec-333 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "333 High income threshold" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this section, the high income threshold is the amount prescribed by, or worked out in the manner prescribed by, the regulations. (2) A regulation made for the purposes of subsection (1) has no effect to the extent that it would have the effect of reducing the amount of the high income threshold. (3) If: (a) in prescribing a manner in which the high income threshold is worked out, regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) specify a particular matter or state of affairs; and (b) as a result of a change in the matter or state of affairs, the amount of the high income threshold worked out in that manner would, but for this subsection, be less than it was on the last occasion on which this subsection did not apply;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "137"^^xsd:integer .

