concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "333D Prohibition on pay secrecy terms"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-333d ;
    values:originalText "An employer contravenes this section if: (a) the employer enters into a contract of employment or other written agreement with an employee; and (b) the contract or agreement includes a term that is inconsistent with subsection 333B(1) or (2) (about employee rights relating to pay secrecy). Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Other terms and conditions of employment  Part 2-9 Fixed term contracts  Division 5 Section 333E Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "An employer contravenes this section if: (a) the employer enters into a contract of employment or other written agreement with an employee; and (b) the contract or agreement includes a term that is inconsistent with subsection 333B(1) or (2) (about employee rights relating to pay secrecy). Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Other terms and conditions of employment  Part 2-9 Fixed term contracts  Division 5 Section 333E Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c489d900c83c1fbda4540905ad026b34016176cf92d7032bd2b827b251b3793a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "140"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer prohibited from including pay secrecy terms in employment contracts." ;
