    cof:title "333M(5) Employee right to disconnect" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) For the avoidance of doubt, an employee’s refusal to monitor, read or respond to contact, or attempted contact, from their employer, or from a third party if the contact or attempted contact relates to their work, will be unreasonable if the contact or attempted contact is required under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory." ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333m-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "333M(6) Employee right to disconnect"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-333m-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) For the avoidance of doubt, if: (a) an employee is covered by an enterprise agreement; and (b) the enterprise agreement includes a right to disconnect term that is more favourable to the employee than the rights in subsections (1) and (2); the right to disconnect term in the agreement continues to apply to the employee. Subdivision B—Disputes about the employee right to disconnect" ;
    skos:definition "(6) For the avoidance of doubt, if: (a) an employee is covered by an enterprise agreement; and (b) the enterprise agreement includes a right to disconnect term that is more favourable to the employee than the rights in subsections (1) and (2); the right to disconnect term in the agreement continues to apply to the employee. Subdivision B—Disputes about the employee right to disconnect"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bf8e0a4c1e449e34ff9e8cac15f244da324b45dcca06b6e353966154e852f678" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333m ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employee right to disconnect prevails over company rights if more favorable" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
