concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "333N Disputes about the employee right to disconnect"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-333n ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if: (a) there is a dispute between an employer and an employee because the employee has refused to monitor, read or respond to contact or attempted contact under subsection 333M(1) or (2) and: (i) the employer reasonably believes that the refusal is unreasonable; or (ii) the employer has asserted that the refusal is unreasonable and the employee reasonably believes the refusal is not unreasonable; or (b) there is another dispute between the employer and the employee about the operation of section 333M.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if: (a) there is a dispute between an employer and an employee because the employee has refused to monitor, read or respond to contact or attempted contact under subsection 333M(1) or (2) and: (i) the employer reasonably believes that the refusal is unreasonable; or (ii) the employer has asserted that the refusal is unreasonable and the employee reasonably believes the refusal is not unreasonable; or (b) there is another dispute between the employer and the employee about the operation of section 333M.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "98e6a821ba5ac139376095c0fa005ae2f1041a6091dce35e7cf6c5a40870bdfe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "149"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333n-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333n-ss-2 ;
