doc:sec-333p-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "333P(2) Orders to stop refusing contact or to stop taking certain" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC may make any order it considers appropriate (other than an order requiring the payment of a pecuniary amount): (a) if the FWC is satisfied that the circumstance set out in paragraph (1)(a) applies—to prevent the employee from continuing to unreasonably refuse to monitor, read or respond to contact or attempted contact; or (b) if the FWC is satisfied that the circumstance set out in subparagraph (1)(b)(i) applies—to prevent the employer from taking the action; or (c) if the FWC is satisfied that the circumstance set out in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) applies—to prevent the employer from continuing to require the employee to monitor, read or respond to contact or attempted contact." ;
    cof:pageNumber "150"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333p-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "333P(3) Orders to stop refusing contact or to stop taking certain"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-333p-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The FWC must: (a) start to deal with an application, to the extent that it consists of an application for an order under this section, within 14 days after the application is made; and (b) deal with the application as soon as is reasonably practicable after the FWC starts to deal with it.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(3) The FWC must: (a) start to deal with an application, to the extent that it consists of an application for an order under this section, within 14 days after the application is made; and (b) deal with the application as soon as is reasonably practicable after the FWC starts to deal with it.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "518706919f2e9e355d57da35676d1e3fd6ee43f2593dc7f08e132743f7c728a1" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-333p ;
    cof:pageNumber "150"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The FWC must deal with an application within 14 days and as soon as reasonably practicable after starting to deal with it." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
