    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if: (a) a child is stillborn or dies; and (b) an employee would have been entitled to leave, under the terms and conditions of the employee’s employment, if the child had not been stillborn or died; and (c) that leave is paid for by the employee’s employer and is associated with: (i) the birth of a child of the employee or the employee’s spouse or de facto partner; or (ii) the placement of a child with the employee for adoption. Note: For the definition of a stillborn child, see subsection 77A(2). Employee must be allowed to take paid parental leave"@en ;
