concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-343 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "343 Coercion"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-343 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person with intent to coerce the other person, or a third person, to: (a) exercise or not exercise, or propose to exercise or not exercise, a workplace right; or (b) exercise, or propose to exercise, a workplace right in a particular way. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to protected industrial action." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person with intent to coerce the other person, or a third person, to: (a) exercise or not exercise, or propose to exercise or not exercise, a workplace right; or (b) exercise, or propose to exercise, a workplace right in a particular way. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to protected industrial action."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "52f131b1b42aec919e80cd3cd0436af3ce441b77cbfa46ab9c83e30eedb33d66" ;
    cof:pageNumber "168"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-343-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-343-ss-2 ;
