doc:sec-343 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "343 Coercion" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person with intent to coerce the other person, or a third person, to: (a) exercise or not exercise, or propose to exercise or not exercise, a workplace right; or (b) exercise, or propose to exercise, a workplace right in a particular way. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to protected industrial action." ;
    cof:pageNumber "168"^^xsd:integer .

