concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-346-logic-alleninterval-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:AllenInterval ;
    cml:operator "Temporal Interval" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Defines the temporal interval for the prohibition." ;
    cml:premiseText "The other person engages, or has at any time engaged or proposed to engage, in industrial activity within the meaning of paragraph 347(a) or (b)." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The temporal interval starts from the engagement in industrial activity." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::interval_reasoning" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-346 cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-346-logic-ltl-5 .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-346-logic-ltl-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "Temporal Interval" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Defines the temporal interval for the prohibition." ;
    cml:premiseText "The other person does not engage, or has at any time not engaged or proposed to not engage, in industrial activity within the meaning of paragraphs 347(c) to (g)." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The temporal interval ends from the non-engagement in industrial activity." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-346 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "346 Protection" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A person must not take adverse action against another person because the other person: (a) is or is not, or was or was not, an officer or member of an industrial association; or (b) engages, or has at any time engaged or proposed to engage, in industrial activity within the meaning of paragraph 347(a) or (b); or (c) does not engage, or has at any time not engaged or proposed to not engage, in industrial activity within the meaning of paragraphs 347(c) to (g). Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-347 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "347 Meaning of engages in industrial activity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-347 ;
    values:originalText "A person engages in industrial activity if the person: (a) becomes or does not become, or remains or ceases to be, an officer or member of an industrial association; or (b) does, or does not: (i) become involved in establishing an industrial association; or (ii) organise or promote a lawful activity for, or on behalf of, an industrial association; or (iii) encourage, or participate in, a lawful activity organised or promoted by an industrial association; or (iv) comply with a lawful request made by, or requirement of, an industrial association; or (v) represent or advance the views, claims or interests of an industrial association; or (vi) pay a fee (however described) to an industrial association, or to someone in lieu of an industrial association; or  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 General protections  Part 3-1 Industrial activities  Division 4 Section 348 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (vii) seek to be represented by an industrial association; or (c) organises or promotes an unlawful activity for, or on behalf of, an industrial association; or (d) encourages, or participates in, an unlawful activity organised or promoted by an industrial association; or (e) complies with an unlawful request made by, or requirement of, an industrial association; or (f) takes part in industrial action; or (g) makes a payment: (i) that, because of Division 9 of Part 3-3 (which deals with payments relating to periods of industrial action), an employer must not pay; or (ii) to which an employee is not entitled because of that Division." ;
    skos:definition "A person engages in industrial activity if the person: (a) becomes or does not become, or remains or ceases to be, an officer or member of an industrial association; or (b) does, or does not: (i) become involved in establishing an industrial association; or (ii) organise or promote a lawful activity for, or on behalf of, an industrial association; or (iii) encourage, or participate in, a lawful activity organised or promoted by an industrial association; or (iv) comply with a lawful request made by, or requirement of, an industrial association; or (v) represent or advance the views, claims or interests of an industrial association; or (vi) pay a fee (however described) to an industrial association, or to someone in lieu of an industrial association; or  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 General protections  Part 3-1 Industrial activities  Division 4 Section 348 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (vii) seek to be represented by an industrial association; or (c) organises or promotes an unlawful activity for, or on behalf of, an industrial association; or (d) encourages, or participates in, an unlawful activity organised or promoted by an industrial association; or (e) complies with an unlawful request made by, or requirement of, an industrial association; or (f) takes part in industrial action; or (g) makes a payment: (i) that, because of Division 9 of Part 3-3 (which deals with payments relating to periods of industrial action), an employer must not pay; or (ii) to which an employee is not entitled because of that Division."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "080e96aac3f3659054c84e4767c5976c487b74f48c0c7b8caaa4b08e4712478e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Engages in industrial activity if meets certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
