concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-350 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "350 Inducements—membership action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-350 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An employer must not induce an employee to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) A person who has entered into a contract for services with an independent contractor must not induce the independent contractor to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2A) A regulated business must not induce a regulated contractor to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (3) A person takes membership action if the person becomes, does not become, remains or ceases to be, an officer or member of an industrial association." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An employer must not induce an employee to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) A person who has entered into a contract for services with an independent contractor must not induce the independent contractor to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2A) A regulated business must not induce a regulated contractor to take, or propose to take, membership action. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (3) A person takes membership action if the person becomes, does not become, remains or ceases to be, an officer or member of an industrial association."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "446bd6a5258752f48a523bb3b50ecd0c39e85504e984f83199107402aff85a86" ;
    cof:pageNumber "172"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-350-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-350-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-350-ss-2a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-350-ss-3 ;
