concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-354 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "354 Coverage by particular instruments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-354 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not discriminate against an employer because: (a) employees of the employer are covered, or not covered, by: (i) provisions of the National Employment Standards; or (ii) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (iii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation; or (b) it is proposed that employees of the employer be covered, or not be covered, by: (i) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (ii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to protected industrial action. (3) A person must not discriminate against a regulated business because: (a) regulated workers in relation to the regulated business are covered, or not covered, by a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (b) it is proposed that regulated workers in relation to the regulated business are covered, or not covered, by a  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 General protections  Part 3-1 Other protections  Division 5 Section 355 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument). Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not discriminate against an employer because: (a) employees of the employer are covered, or not covered, by: (i) provisions of the National Employment Standards; or (ii) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (iii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation; or (b) it is proposed that employees of the employer be covered, or not be covered, by: (i) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (ii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to protected industrial action. (3) A person must not discriminate against a regulated business because: (a) regulated workers in relation to the regulated business are covered, or not covered, by a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (b) it is proposed that regulated workers in relation to the regulated business are covered, or not covered, by a  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 General protections  Part 3-1 Other protections  Division 5 Section 355 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument). Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "abdb43c5fb3b8943be4fdf434fdc23215bc3b6f0b1379fd51e9db805f77c001f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-354-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-354-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-354-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
