doc:sec-354-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "354(1) Coverage by particular instruments" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not discriminate against an employer because: (a) employees of the employer are covered, or not covered, by: (i) provisions of the National Employment Standards; or (ii) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (iii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation; or (b) it is proposed that employees of the employer be covered, or not be covered, by: (i) a particular type of workplace instrument (including a particular kind of workplace instrument within a type of workplace instrument); or (ii) an enterprise agreement that does, or does not, cover an employee organisation, or a particular employee organisation. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer .

