concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-374 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "374 Conferences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-374 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) an application is made under section 372; and (b) the parties to the dispute agree to participate; the FWC must conduct a conference to deal with the dispute. Note 1: For conferences, see section 592. Note 2: The FWC may deal with a dispute by mediation or conciliation, or by making a recommendation or expressing an opinion (see subsection 595(2)). (2) Despite subsection 592(3), the FWC must conduct the conference in private." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If: (a) an application is made under section 372; and (b) the parties to the dispute agree to participate; the FWC must conduct a conference to deal with the dispute. Note 1: For conferences, see section 592. Note 2: The FWC may deal with a dispute by mediation or conciliation, or by making a recommendation or expressing an opinion (see subsection 595(2)). (2) Despite subsection 592(3), the FWC must conduct the conference in private."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "03ee69c5883f4084ac4c73ca62ddabd20dc8ec3a08968550acf337fae5cf3297" ;
    cof:pageNumber "189"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-374-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-374-ss-2 ;
