concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-389 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "389 Meaning of genuine redundancy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-389 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person’s dismissal was a case of genuine redundancy if: (a) the person’s employer no longer required the person’s job to be performed by anyone because of changes in the operational requirements of the employer’s enterprise; and (b) the employer has complied with any obligation in a modern award or enterprise agreement that applied to the employment to consult about the redundancy. (2) A person’s dismissal was not a case of genuine redundancy if it would have been reasonable in all the circumstances for the person to be redeployed within: (a) the employer’s enterprise; or (b) the enterprise of an associated entity of the employer.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person’s dismissal was a case of genuine redundancy if: (a) the person’s employer no longer required the person’s job to be performed by anyone because of changes in the operational requirements of the employer’s enterprise; and (b) the employer has complied with any obligation in a modern award or enterprise agreement that applied to the employment to consult about the redundancy. (2) A person’s dismissal was not a case of genuine redundancy if it would have been reasonable in all the circumstances for the person to be redeployed within: (a) the employer’s enterprise; or (b) the enterprise of an associated entity of the employer.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0a55c7917b6a64491014c9458a9d18492be0f617b8104e6a4f5746adab3b4d15" ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-389-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-389-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
