doc:sec-414-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "414(1) Notice requirements for industrial action" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before a person engages in employee claim action for a proposed enterprise agreement, a bargaining representative of an employee who will be covered by the agreement must give written notice of the action to the employer of the employee." ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-414-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "414(2) Notice requirements for industrial action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-414-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The period of notice must be at least: (a) subject to paragraph (b):  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected industrial action  Division 2 Section 414 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (i) if subparagraph (ii) of this paragraph does not apply—3 working days; or (ii) if the proposed enterprise agreement is a multi-enterprise agreement—120 hours; or (b) if a protected action ballot order for the employee claim action specifies a longer period of notice for the purposes of this paragraph—that period of notice. Note: For a proposed cooperative workplace agreement, see subsection 413(2). Notice of employee claim action not to be given until ballot results declared" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The period of notice must be at least: (a) subject to paragraph (b):  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected industrial action  Division 2 Section 414 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (i) if subparagraph (ii) of this paragraph does not apply—3 working days; or (ii) if the proposed enterprise agreement is a multi-enterprise agreement—120 hours; or (b) if a protected action ballot order for the employee claim action specifies a longer period of notice for the purposes of this paragraph—that period of notice. Note: For a proposed cooperative workplace agreement, see subsection 413(2). Notice of employee claim action not to be given until ballot results declared"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b2d1993ecbda55f60667bf9aeade9a05a89f925bd91507bee3a6cd926907ea77" ;
