concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-414-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "414(5) Notice requirements for industrial action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-414-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Before an employer engages in employer response action for a proposed enterprise agreement, the employer must: (a) give written notice of the action to each bargaining representative of an employee who will be covered by the agreement; and (b) take all reasonable steps to notify the employees who will be covered by the agreement of the action. Notice requirements—content" ;
    skos:definition "(5) Before an employer engages in employer response action for a proposed enterprise agreement, the employer must: (a) give written notice of the action to each bargaining representative of an employee who will be covered by the agreement; and (b) take all reasonable steps to notify the employees who will be covered by the agreement of the action. Notice requirements—content"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea6d5ccacb0ddb43237ce6353398c4d0fa74dba1658c10b053c56b097d943354" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-414 ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must give written notice to bargaining representatives and employees before engaging in employer response action." ;
