concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-421 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "421 Contravening an order etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-421 ;
    values:originalText "Contravening orders (1) A person to whom an order under section 418, 419 or 420 applies must not contravene a term of the order. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) However, a person is not required to comply with an order if: (a) the order is an order under section 418, or an order under section 420 that relates to an application for an order under section 418; and (b) the industrial action to which the order relates is, or would be, protected industrial action.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "Contravening orders (1) A person to whom an order under section 418, 419 or 420 applies must not contravene a term of the order. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) However, a person is not required to comply with an order if: (a) the order is an order under section 418, or an order under section 420 that relates to an application for an order under section 418; and (b) the industrial action to which the order relates is, or would be, protected industrial action.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "56a4ebe98e48e0ff0bc6a90f8639c78dba4bc6005b0591eb5b13237d36ba2a2a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "225"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-421-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-421-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.225" .
