doc:sec-437-ss-2a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "437(2A) Application for a protected action ballot order" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2A) Subsection (1) does not apply unless there has been a notification time in relation to the proposed enterprise agreement. Note: For notification time, see subsection 173(2). Protected industrial action cannot be taken until after bargaining has commenced (including where the scope of the proposed enterprise agreement is the only matter in dispute). Matters to be specified in application" ;
    cof:pageNumber "240"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-437-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "437(3) Application for a protected action ballot order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-437-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The application must specify: (a) the group or groups of employees who are to be balloted; and (b) the question or questions to be put to the employees who are to be balloted, including the nature of the proposed industrial action; and (c) the name of the person or entity that the applicant wishes to be the protected action ballot agent for the protected action ballot.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 437A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Note: The protected action ballot agent for the ballot must be an eligible protected action ballot agent unless there are exceptional circumstances: see section 444." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The application must specify: (a) the group or groups of employees who are to be balloted; and (b) the question or questions to be put to the employees who are to be balloted, including the nature of the proposed industrial action; and (c) the name of the person or entity that the applicant wishes to be the protected action ballot agent for the protected action ballot.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 437A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Note: The protected action ballot agent for the ballot must be an eligible protected action ballot agent unless there are exceptional circumstances: see section 444."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "68b12541db2efb452bf0d92df98c88fcf1bb5e201d1a1779e2bc2ac82d4235fc" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-437 ;
    cof:pageNumber "240"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application requirements for a protected action ballot order" ;
    dc:description "The application must specify the group or groups of employees, questions to be put to the employees, and the name of the person or entity that wishes to be the protected action ballot agent." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.240" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-437-ss-3-norm .
