doc:sec-445 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "445 Notice of protected action ballot order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "As soon as practicable after making a protected action ballot order, the FWC must give a copy of the order to: (a) each applicant for the order; and (b) the employer of the employees who are to be balloted; and (c) the protected action ballot agent for the protected action ballot." ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-446 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "446 Protected action ballot order may require 2 or more protected"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-446 ;
    values:originalText "action ballots to be held at the same time (1) This section applies if:  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 447 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) the FWC has made a protected action ballot order; and (b) the FWC proposes to make another protected action ballot order or orders; and (c) the orders would require a protected action ballot to be held in relation to industrial action by employees of the same employer or employees at the same workplace. (2) The FWC may make, or vary, the protected action ballot orders so as to require the protected action ballots to be held at the same time if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the level of disruption of the employer’s enterprise, or at the workplace, could be reduced if the ballots were held at the same time; and (b) that requiring the ballots to be held at the same time will not unreasonably delay either ballot." ;
    skos:definition "action ballots to be held at the same time (1) This section applies if:  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 447 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) the FWC has made a protected action ballot order; and (b) the FWC proposes to make another protected action ballot order or orders; and (c) the orders would require a protected action ballot to be held in relation to industrial action by employees of the same employer or employees at the same workplace. (2) The FWC may make, or vary, the protected action ballot orders so as to require the protected action ballots to be held at the same time if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the level of disruption of the employer’s enterprise, or at the workplace, could be reduced if the ballots were held at the same time; and (b) that requiring the ballots to be held at the same time will not unreasonably delay either ballot."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8dea35f7d13047d34786c58d4376f6c37995ad1bd0cdda421e65581e85035bd7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-446-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-446-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.246" .
doc:sec-446 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "446 Protected action ballot order may require 2 or more protected" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "action ballots to be held at the same time (1) This section applies if:  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 447 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) the FWC has made a protected action ballot order; and (b) the FWC proposes to make another protected action ballot order or orders; and (c) the orders would require a protected action ballot to be held in relation to industrial action by employees of the same employer or employees at the same workplace. (2) The FWC may make, or vary, the protected action ballot orders so as to require the protected action ballots to be held at the same time if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the level of disruption of the employer’s enterprise, or at the workplace, could be reduced if the ballots were held at the same time; and (b) that requiring the ballots to be held at the same time will not unreasonably delay either ballot." ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer .

