doc:sec-446-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "446(2) Protected action ballot order may require 2 or more protected" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC may make, or vary, the protected action ballot orders so as to require the protected action ballots to be held at the same time if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the level of disruption of the employer’s enterprise, or at the workplace, could be reduced if the ballots were held at the same time; and (b) that requiring the ballots to be held at the same time will not unreasonably delay either ballot." ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-447 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "447 Variation of protected action ballot order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-447 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An applicant for a protected action ballot order may apply to the FWC to vary the order. (2) The protected action ballot agent for a protected action ballot may apply to the FWC to vary the protected action ballot order to change the date by which voting in the ballot closes. (3) An application may be made under subsection (1) or (2): (a) at any time before the date by which voting in the protected action ballot closes; or (b) if the ballot has not been held before that date and the FWC consents—after that time. (4) If an application is made under subsection (1) or (2), the FWC may vary the protected action ballot order.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An applicant for a protected action ballot order may apply to the FWC to vary the order. (2) The protected action ballot agent for a protected action ballot may apply to the FWC to vary the protected action ballot order to change the date by which voting in the ballot closes. (3) An application may be made under subsection (1) or (2): (a) at any time before the date by which voting in the protected action ballot closes; or (b) if the ballot has not been held before that date and the FWC consents—after that time. (4) If an application is made under subsection (1) or (2), the FWC may vary the protected action ballot order.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "89c613f0bc62029f9219e4bd246d71be0e9561176751bf308671914c85be30e8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "247"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-447-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-447-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-447-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-447-ss-4 ;
