concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1 cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2 .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:AllenInterval ;
    cml:operator "Overlaps" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Temporal overlap with declaration period" ;
    cml:premiseText "(d) the action commences: (i) during the 30-day period starting on the date of the declaration of the results of the ballot; or (ii) if the FWC has extended that period under subsection (3)—during the extended period." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The action must occur within a specified time frame." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::interval_reasoning" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1 cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-ltl-3 .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-ltl-3 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "Until" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Temporal relationship with declaration period" ;
    cml:premiseText "(d) the action commences: (i) during the 30-day period starting on the date of the declaration of the results of the ballot; or (ii) if the FWC has extended that period under subsection (3)—during the extended period." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The action occurs until a specified time frame." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1 cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4 .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Diffusion ;
    cml:operator "Diffuses" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Spread of authorization to employees" ;
    cml:premiseText "(a) the action was the subject of the ballot; and (b) at least 50% of the employees on the roll of voters for the ballot voted in the ballot." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The authorization spreads to a significant portion of employees." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::diffusion" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1 cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-argumentation-5 .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-1-logic-argumentation-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Argumentation ;
    cml:operator "Implication" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Relationship between action and ballot outcome" ;
    cml:premiseText "(c) more than 50% of the valid votes were votes approving the action; and (d) the action commences: (i) during the 30-day period starting on the date of the declaration of the results of the ballot; or (ii) if the FWC has extended that period under subsection (3)—during the extended period." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The action is approved by a majority of votes if it occurs within the specified time frame." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::argumentation" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-459-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "459(1) Circumstances in which industrial action is authorised by" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Industrial action by employees is authorised by a protected action ballot if: (a) the action was the subject of the ballot; and (b) at least 50% of the employees on the roll of voters for the ballot voted in the ballot; and  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Protected action ballots  Division 8 Section 460 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (c) more than 50% of the valid votes were votes approving the action; and (d) the action commences: (i) during the 30-day period starting on the date of the declaration of the results of the ballot; or (ii) if the FWC has extended that period under subsection (3)—during the extended period. Note: Under Division 2, industrial action by employees for a proposed enterprise agreement (other than employee response action) is not protected industrial action unless it has been authorised in advance by a protected action ballot." ;
    cof:pageNumber "256"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "459(2) Circumstances in which industrial action is authorised by"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-459-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If: (a) the nature of the proposed industrial action specified in the question or questions put to the employees in the protected action ballot included periods of industrial action of a particular duration; and (b) the question or questions did not specify that consecutive periods of that industrial action may be organised or engaged in; then only the first period in a series of consecutive periods of that industrial action is the subject of the ballot for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If: (a) the nature of the proposed industrial action specified in the question or questions put to the employees in the protected action ballot included periods of industrial action of a particular duration; and (b) the question or questions did not specify that consecutive periods of that industrial action may be organised or engaged in; then only the first period in a series of consecutive periods of that industrial action is the subject of the ballot for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8dcc8792e10bb1056d7ec6a4e9221b62df0e73f8a4d4852174ebe5604ed73871" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-459 ;
    cof:pageNumber "256"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Industrial action is authorised under specific circumstances." ;
