doc:sec-462 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "462 Interferences etc. with protected action ballot" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "General (1) A person (the first person) must not do any of the following in relation to a protected action ballot: (a) hinder or obstruct the holding of the ballot; (b) use any form of intimidation to prevent a person entitled to vote in the ballot from voting, or to influence the vote of such a person; (c) threaten, offer or suggest, or use, cause or inflict, any violence, injury, punishment, damage, loss or disadvantage because of, or to induce: (i) any vote or omission to vote; or (ii) any support of, or opposition to, voting in a particular manner; (d) offer an advantage (whether financial or otherwise) to a person entitled to vote in the ballot because of or to induce: (i) any vote or omission to vote; or (ii) any support of, or opposition to, voting in a particular manner; (e) counsel or advise a person entitled to vote to refrain from voting; (f) impersonate another person to obtain a ballot paper to which the first person is not entitled, or impersonate another person for the purpose of voting; (g) do an act that results in a ballot paper or envelope being destroyed, defaced, altered, taken or otherwise interfered with; (h) fraudulently put a paper ballot paper or other paper: (i) into a repository that serves to receive or hold paper ballot papers; or (ii) into the post;  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "259"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-464 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "464 Costs of protected action ballot conducted by the Australian"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-464 ;
    values:originalText "Electoral Commission (1) This section applies if the protected action ballot agent for a protected action ballot is the Australian Electoral Commission. (2) The Commonwealth is liable for the costs incurred by the Australian Electoral Commission in relation to the protected action ballot, whether or not the ballot is completed. (3) However, except as provided by regulations made for the purposes of subsection 466(1), the Commonwealth is not liable for any costs incurred by the Australian Electoral Commission in relation to  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "Electoral Commission (1) This section applies if the protected action ballot agent for a protected action ballot is the Australian Electoral Commission. (2) The Commonwealth is liable for the costs incurred by the Australian Electoral Commission in relation to the protected action ballot, whether or not the ballot is completed. (3) However, except as provided by regulations made for the purposes of subsection 466(1), the Commonwealth is not liable for any costs incurred by the Australian Electoral Commission in relation to  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5dbeaa858295962fd6e6fa4fb2f351966e8b76771cc93d8d1363e6279df823f9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "261"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-464-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-464-ss-2 ;
