doc:sec-471 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "471 Payments relating to partial work bans" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Employer gives notice of reduction in payments (1) If: (a) an employee engaged, or engages, in protected industrial action against an employer on a day; and (b) the industrial action is a partial work ban; and (c) the employer gives to the employee a written notice stating that, because of the ban, the employee’s payments will be reduced by a proportion specified in the notice; then the employee’s payments are reduced in accordance with subsection (2) in relation to the period (the industrial action period) referred to in subsection (5). (2) The employee’s payments in relation to the industrial action period are reduced: (a) by the proportion specified in the notice; or (b) if the FWC has ordered a different proportion under section 472—by the proportion specified in the order; and the modern award, enterprise agreement or contract of employment that applies to the employee’s employment has effect accordingly. (3) The regulations may prescribe how the proportion referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is to be worked out. Employer gives notice of non-payment (4) If: (a) an employee engaged, or engages, in protected industrial action against an employer on a day; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "267"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-471-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "471(1) Payments relating to partial work bans"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-471-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) an employee engaged, or engages, in protected industrial action against an employer on a day; and (b) the industrial action is a partial work ban; and (c) the employer gives to the employee a written notice stating that, because of the ban, the employee’s payments will be reduced by a proportion specified in the notice; then the employee’s payments are reduced in accordance with subsection (2) in relation to the period (the industrial action period) referred to in subsection (5)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If: (a) an employee engaged, or engages, in protected industrial action against an employer on a day; and (b) the industrial action is a partial work ban; and (c) the employer gives to the employee a written notice stating that, because of the ban, the employee’s payments will be reduced by a proportion specified in the notice; then the employee’s payments are reduced in accordance with subsection (2) in relation to the period (the industrial action period) referred to in subsection (5)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "357f5c72cac7d9ddcb3d781e8c29c9a26f7e3f97a52b4929540aab7dba0590d1" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-471 ;
    cof:pageNumber "267"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employee's payments reduced due to partial work ban" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
