    values:originalText "(2) An employee organisation, or an officer or member of an employee organisation, must not ask an employer to make a payment to an employee if the employer would contravene section 470 by making the payment. Note 1: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). Note 2: Acts of coercion, or misrepresentations, relating to such payments may also contravene section 348 or 349.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Payments relating to periods of industrial action  Division 9 Section 474 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Subdivision B—Industrial action that is not protected industrial action" ;
    skos:definition "(2) An employee organisation, or an officer or member of an employee organisation, must not ask an employer to make a payment to an employee if the employer would contravene section 470 by making the payment. Note 1: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). Note 2: Acts of coercion, or misrepresentations, relating to such payments may also contravene section 348 or 349.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Payments relating to periods of industrial action  Division 9 Section 474 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Subdivision B—Industrial action that is not protected industrial action"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d96622aec7ec09a2b8a2fdce02d981cf34e1546ed120b11bead3ed3606561fcd" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-473 ;
