doc:sec-473-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "473(2) Accepting or seeking payments relating to periods of industrial" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An employee organisation, or an officer or member of an employee organisation, must not ask an employer to make a payment to an employee if the employer would contravene section 470 by making the payment. Note 1: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). Note 2: Acts of coercion, or misrepresentations, relating to such payments may also contravene section 348 or 349.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Industrial action  Part 3-3 Payments relating to periods of industrial action  Division 9 Section 474 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Subdivision B—Industrial action that is not protected industrial action" ;
    cof:pageNumber "270"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-474 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 Payments not to be made relating to certain periods of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-474 ;
    values:originalText "industrial action (1) If an employee engaged, or engages, in industrial action that is not protected industrial action against an employer on a day, the employer must not make a payment to an employee in relation to: (a) if the total duration of the industrial action on that day is at least 4 hours—the total duration of the industrial action on that day; or (b) otherwise—4 hours of that day. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) However, if the industrial action is, or includes, an overtime ban, this section does not apply, in relation to a period of overtime to which the ban applies, unless: (a) the employer requested or required the employee to work the period of overtime; and (b) the employee refused to work the period of overtime; and (c) the refusal was a contravention of the employee’s obligations under a modern award, enterprise agreement or contract of employment. Note: An employee is able to refuse to work additional hours if they are unreasonable (see subsection 62(2)). There may be other circumstances in which an employee can lawfully refuse to work additional hours. (2A) If: (a) the industrial action is, or includes, an overtime ban; and (b) this section applies in relation to a period of overtime to which the ban applies; then, for the purposes of this section: (c) the total duration of the industrial action is, or includes, the period of overtime to which the ban applies; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "industrial action (1) If an employee engaged, or engages, in industrial action that is not protected industrial action against an employer on a day, the employer must not make a payment to an employee in relation to: (a) if the total duration of the industrial action on that day is at least 4 hours—the total duration of the industrial action on that day; or (b) otherwise—4 hours of that day. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) However, if the industrial action is, or includes, an overtime ban, this section does not apply, in relation to a period of overtime to which the ban applies, unless: (a) the employer requested or required the employee to work the period of overtime; and (b) the employee refused to work the period of overtime; and (c) the refusal was a contravention of the employee’s obligations under a modern award, enterprise agreement or contract of employment. Note: An employee is able to refuse to work additional hours if they are unreasonable (see subsection 62(2)). There may be other circumstances in which an employee can lawfully refuse to work additional hours. (2A) If: (a) the industrial action is, or includes, an overtime ban; and (b) this section applies in relation to a period of overtime to which the ban applies; then, for the purposes of this section: (c) the total duration of the industrial action is, or includes, the period of overtime to which the ban applies; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f87d1ffb394267b233f891c777032453099aa56b2fe08bb0d0f1d7573675497b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "271"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-474-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-474-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-474-ss-2a ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
