concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-483 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "483 Later access to record or document"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-483 ;
    values:originalText "Later access to record or document (1) The permit holder may, by written notice, require an affected employer to produce, or provide access to, a record or document (other than a non-member record or document) that is directly relevant to the suspected contravention on a later day or days specified in the notice. (1A) However, an affected employer is not required under subsection (1) to produce, or provide access to, a record or document if to do so would contravene a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "Later access to record or document (1) The permit holder may, by written notice, require an affected employer to produce, or provide access to, a record or document (other than a non-member record or document) that is directly relevant to the suspected contravention on a later day or days specified in the notice. (1A) However, an affected employer is not required under subsection (1) to produce, or provide access to, a record or document if to do so would contravene a law of the Commonwealth or a law of a State or Territory.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "813414e35235438bda9ccf7e936ac81ae4604e4e7cf9f5a26e38fbd97056e18e" ;
