concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-503 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "503 Misrepresentations about things authorised by this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-503 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not take action: (a) with the intention of giving the impression; or (b) reckless as to whether the impression is given; that the doing of a thing is authorised by this Part if it is not so authorised. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person reasonably believes that the doing of the thing is authorised." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not take action: (a) with the intention of giving the impression; or (b) reckless as to whether the impression is given; that the doing of a thing is authorised by this Part if it is not so authorised. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person reasonably believes that the doing of the thing is authorised."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3d5adef0323b3463ffa4e7ac76351a60b8d0b525559180a75a66e40ac34bdee3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "297"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-503-ss-1 ;
