concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-518 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "518 Entry notice requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-518 ;
    values:originalText "Requirements for all entry notices (1) An entry notice must specify the following: (a) the premises that are proposed to be entered; (b) the day of the entry; (c) the organisation of which the permit holder for the entry is an official.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Right of entry  Part 3-4 Entry permits, entry notices and certificates  Division 6 Section 518 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Requirements for entry notice for entry to investigate suspected contravention (2) An entry notice given for an entry under section 481, 483A or 483D must: (a) specify that section as the provision that authorises the entry; and (b) unless the entry is a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A—specify the particulars of the suspected contravention, or contraventions; and (c) for an entry under section 481—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a member, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (ca) for an entry under section 483A other than a designated outworker terms entry—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a TCF award worker, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (cb) for a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A— contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of TCF award workers; and (cc) for an entry under section 483D—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a TCF award worker: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "Requirements for all entry notices (1) An entry notice must specify the following: (a) the premises that are proposed to be entered; (b) the day of the entry; (c) the organisation of which the permit holder for the entry is an official.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Right of entry  Part 3-4 Entry permits, entry notices and certificates  Division 6 Section 518 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Requirements for entry notice for entry to investigate suspected contravention (2) An entry notice given for an entry under section 481, 483A or 483D must: (a) specify that section as the provision that authorises the entry; and (b) unless the entry is a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A—specify the particulars of the suspected contravention, or contraventions; and (c) for an entry under section 481—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a member, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (ca) for an entry under section 483A other than a designated outworker terms entry—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a TCF award worker, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (cb) for a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A— contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of TCF award workers; and (cc) for an entry under section 483D—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "56e10e84de58fac1d538374f7693709af11e269d8183eb77aa7684f7bc621fa8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "310"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-518-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-518-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.310" .
doc:sec-518 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "518 Entry notice requirements" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Requirements for all entry notices (1) An entry notice must specify the following: (a) the premises that are proposed to be entered; (b) the day of the entry; (c) the organisation of which the permit holder for the entry is an official.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Right of entry  Part 3-4 Entry permits, entry notices and certificates  Division 6 Section 518 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Requirements for entry notice for entry to investigate suspected contravention (2) An entry notice given for an entry under section 481, 483A or 483D must: (a) specify that section as the provision that authorises the entry; and (b) unless the entry is a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A—specify the particulars of the suspected contravention, or contraventions; and (c) for an entry under section 481—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a member, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (ca) for an entry under section 483A other than a designated outworker terms entry—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a TCF award worker, who performs work on the premises, and: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or (ii) who is affected by the suspected contravention or contraventions; and (cb) for a designated outworker terms entry under section 483A— contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of TCF award workers; and (cc) for an entry under section 483D—contain a declaration by the permit holder for the entry that the permit holder’s organisation is entitled to represent the industrial interests of a TCF award worker: (i) to whom the suspected contravention or contraventions relate; or  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "310"^^xsd:integer .

