doc:sec-519-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "519(1) Exemption certificates" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC must issue a certificate (an exemption certificate) to an organisation for an entry under section 481 (which deals with entry to investigate suspected contraventions) if: (a) the organisation has applied for the certificate; and (b) either: (i) the FWC reasonably believes that advance notice of the entry given by an entry notice might result in the destruction, concealment or alteration of relevant evidence; or (ii) the FWC is satisfied that the suspected contravention, or contraventions, involve the underpayment of wages, or  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Right of entry  Part 3-4 Entry permits, entry notices and certificates  Division 6 Section 520 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 other monetary entitlements, of a member of the organisation whose industrial interests the organisation is entitled to represent and who performs work on the premises, and the FWC reasonably believes that advance notice of the entry given by an entry notice would hinder an effective investigation into the suspected contravention or contraventions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "312"^^xsd:integer .

