doc:sec-521 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "521 Regulations dealing with instruments under this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The regulations may provide for, and in relation to, the following: (a) the form of entry permits, entry notices, exemption certificates and affected member certificates; (b) additional information to be included on, or given with, entry permits, entry notices, exemption certificates and affected member certificates; (c) the manner in which entry permits, entry notices, exemption certificates and affected member certificates are to be given; (d) any other matter in relation to entry permits, entry notices, exemption certificates and affected member certificates.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Right of entry  Part 3-4 Accommodation and transport arrangements in remote areas  Division 7 Section 521A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "314"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-521a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "521A Meaning of accommodation arrangement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-521a ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) an occupier of premises enters into an arrangement with an organisation; and (b) under the terms of the arrangement, a permit holder is provided with accommodation for the purpose of assisting him or her to exercise rights under this Part; the arrangement is an accommodation arrangement. (2) If: (a) an occupier of premises enters into an arrangement with a permit holder; and (b) under the terms of the arrangement, the permit holder is provided with accommodation for the purpose of assisting him or her to exercise rights under this Part; the arrangement is an accommodation arrangement." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If: (a) an occupier of premises enters into an arrangement with an organisation; and (b) under the terms of the arrangement, a permit holder is provided with accommodation for the purpose of assisting him or her to exercise rights under this Part; the arrangement is an accommodation arrangement. (2) If: (a) an occupier of premises enters into an arrangement with a permit holder; and (b) under the terms of the arrangement, the permit holder is provided with accommodation for the purpose of assisting him or her to exercise rights under this Part; the arrangement is an accommodation arrangement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "24d0ef1b4f38479da2f2c00b74caadf1bacbdffabe2598296123872732e58ef9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "315"^^xsd:integer ;
