doc:sec-527 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "527 Contravening an FWC order dealing with a dispute about the" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "operation of this Part A person must not contravene a term of an FWC order dealing with a dispute about the operation of this Part. Note: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work  Part 3-5A Introduction  Division 1 Section 527A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "322"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "527A Guide to this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-527a ;
    values:originalText "This Part makes it unlawful for a person to sexually harass another person, where: (a) the other person is a worker in a business or undertaking, seeking to become a worker in a particular business or undertaking, or conducting a business or undertaking; and (b) the harassment occurs in connection with the other person being a person of the relevant kind. Persons may be liable for acts contravening this Part that are performed by their employees or agents. Applications may be made to the FWC to deal with a dispute about an alleged contravention of this Part, including by making a stop sexual harassment order. In most cases, a dispute about an alleged contravention of this Part will be dealt with by a court only if the dispute has not been resolved by the FWC." ;
    skos:definition "This Part makes it unlawful for a person to sexually harass another person, where: (a) the other person is a worker in a business or undertaking, seeking to become a worker in a particular business or undertaking, or conducting a business or undertaking; and (b) the harassment occurs in connection with the other person being a person of the relevant kind. Persons may be liable for acts contravening this Part that are performed by their employees or agents. Applications may be made to the FWC to deal with a dispute about an alleged contravention of this Part, including by making a stop sexual harassment order. In most cases, a dispute about an alleged contravention of this Part will be dealt with by a court only if the dispute has not been resolved by the FWC."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6aebdf8bf5919606300ebd71cd8da2cc3ef9f69b0a02105ad93e58a3ccf7648e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "323"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Sexual harassment is prohibited in certain situations." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.323" ;
