concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527ca-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "527CA(2) Concurrent operation of State and Territory laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-527ca-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part does not exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory to the extent that: (a) the law makes an act or omission: (i) an offence; or (ii) subject to a civil penalty; and (b) that (or any similar) act or omission constitutes a contravention of a civil remedy provision of this Part.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work  Part 3-5A Introduction  Division 1 Section 527CA Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part does not exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory to the extent that: (a) the law makes an act or omission: (i) an offence; or (ii) subject to a civil penalty; and (b) that (or any similar) act or omission constitutes a contravention of a civil remedy provision of this Part.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work  Part 3-5A Introduction  Division 1 Section 527CA Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3ababb3ebe71995d220a289741b72027f50b56eacca23ebb6f03ef99923318a8" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527ca ;
