doc:sec-527ca-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "527CA(2) Concurrent operation of State and Territory laws" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part does not exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory to the extent that: (a) the law makes an act or omission: (i) an offence; or (ii) subject to a civil penalty; and (b) that (or any similar) act or omission constitutes a contravention of a civil remedy provision of this Part.  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc.  Chapter 3 Prohibiting sexual harassment in connection with work  Part 3-5A Introduction  Division 1 Section 527CA Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "324"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527ca-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "527CA(3) Concurrent operation of State and Territory laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-527ca-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part does not exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory to the extent that the law allows an application to be made to a person, court or body: (a) for an order or other direction (however described) to prevent a person from being sexually harassed; or (b) to deal with a dispute relating to an allegation that a person has been sexually harassed (whether or not by arbitration). For this purpose, it is irrelevant whether: (c) sexual harassment has a different meaning for the purposes of the law to the meaning it has for the purposes of this Act; or (d) the law describes the conduct prevented, or to which the dispute relates, as sexual harassment. Note 1: An order made under this Part, or under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to a contravention of this Part, will prevail over any order or other direction made by a person, court or body under a law of a State or Territory, to the extent of any inconsistency. Note 2: Generally, section 734B prevents multiple applications or complaints under both this Act and State and Territory anti-discrimination laws in relation to the same conduct." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part does not exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory to the extent that the law allows an application to be made to a person, court or body: (a) for an order or other direction (however described) to prevent a person from being sexually harassed; or (b) to deal with a dispute relating to an allegation that a person has been sexually harassed (whether or not by arbitration). For this purpose, it is irrelevant whether: (c) sexual harassment has a different meaning for the purposes of the law to the meaning it has for the purposes of this Act; or (d) the law describes the conduct prevented, or to which the dispute relates, as sexual harassment. Note 1: An order made under this Part, or under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to a contravention of this Part, will prevail over any order or other direction made by a person, court or body under a law of a State or Territory, to the extent of any inconsistency. Note 2: Generally, section 734B prevents multiple applications or complaints under both this Act and State and Territory anti-discrimination laws in relation to the same conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6122954f7a4fc4c2b6a2413847e5e673a9acb727cbb55dc6528739ef0a87a077" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527ca ;
    cof:pageNumber "324"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Allowing concurrent operation of State and Territory laws to prevent sexual harassment or deal with disputes related to it." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.324" ;
