doc:sec-527g a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "527G Time for application" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The FWC may dismiss an application that is made under section 527F more than 24 months after the contravention, or the  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "329"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-527h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "527H Application fees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-527h ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application to the FWC under section 527F must be accompanied by any fee prescribed by the regulations. (2) The regulations may prescribe: (a) a fee for making an application to the FWC under section 527F; and (b) a method for indexing the fee; and (c) the circumstances in which all or part of the fee may be waived or refunded. Subdivision B—Stop sexual harassment orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application to the FWC under section 527F must be accompanied by any fee prescribed by the regulations. (2) The regulations may prescribe: (a) a fee for making an application to the FWC under section 527F; and (b) a method for indexing the fee; and (c) the circumstances in which all or part of the fee may be waived or refunded. Subdivision B—Stop sexual harassment orders"@en ;
