concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-531 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "531 FWC may make orders where failure to notify or consult"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-531 ;
    values:originalText "registered employee associations about dismissals (1) The FWC may make an order under subsection 532(1) if it is satisfied that: (a) an employer has decided to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological, structural or similar nature, or for reasons including such reasons; and (b) the employer has not complied with subsection (2) (which deals with notifying relevant registered employee associations) or subsection (3) (which deals with consulting relevant registered employee associations); and (c) the employer could reasonably be expected to have known, when he or she made the decision, that one or more of the employees were members of a registered employee association. Notifying relevant registered employee associations (2) An employer complies with this subsection if: (a) the employer notifies each registered employee association of which any of the employees was a member, and that was entitled to represent the industrial interests of that member, of the following: (i) the proposed dismissals and the reasons for them; (ii) the number and categories of employees likely to be affected; (iii) the time when, or the period over which, the employer intends to carry out the dismissals; and (b) the notice is given: (i) as soon as practicable after making the decision; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "registered employee associations about dismissals (1) The FWC may make an order under subsection 532(1) if it is satisfied that: (a) an employer has decided to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological, structural or similar nature, or for reasons including such reasons; and (b) the employer has not complied with subsection (2) (which deals with notifying relevant registered employee associations) or subsection (3) (which deals with consulting relevant registered employee associations); and (c) the employer could reasonably be expected to have known, when he or she made the decision, that one or more of the employees were members of a registered employee association. Notifying relevant registered employee associations (2) An employer complies with this subsection if: (a) the employer notifies each registered employee association of which any of the employees was a member, and that was entitled to represent the industrial interests of that member, of the following: (i) the proposed dismissals and the reasons for them; (ii) the number and categories of employees likely to be affected; (iii) the time when, or the period over which, the employer intends to carry out the dismissals; and (b) the notice is given: (i) as soon as practicable after making the decision; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ca03f17412e6e684a7e63148c31e52cc8d2bf133c9bef7f99ecbe94efadbf54f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "341"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-531-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-531-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.341" .
doc:sec-531 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "531 FWC may make orders where failure to notify or consult" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "registered employee associations about dismissals (1) The FWC may make an order under subsection 532(1) if it is satisfied that: (a) an employer has decided to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological, structural or similar nature, or for reasons including such reasons; and (b) the employer has not complied with subsection (2) (which deals with notifying relevant registered employee associations) or subsection (3) (which deals with consulting relevant registered employee associations); and (c) the employer could reasonably be expected to have known, when he or she made the decision, that one or more of the employees were members of a registered employee association. Notifying relevant registered employee associations (2) An employer complies with this subsection if: (a) the employer notifies each registered employee association of which any of the employees was a member, and that was entitled to represent the industrial interests of that member, of the following: (i) the proposed dismissals and the reasons for them; (ii) the number and categories of employees likely to be affected; (iii) the time when, or the period over which, the employer intends to carry out the dismissals; and (b) the notice is given: (i) as soon as practicable after making the decision; and  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "341"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-531-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "531(1) FWC may make orders where failure to notify or consult"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-531-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may make an order under subsection 532(1) if it is satisfied that: (a) an employer has decided to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological, structural or similar nature, or for reasons including such reasons; and (b) the employer has not complied with subsection (2) (which deals with notifying relevant registered employee associations) or subsection (3) (which deals with consulting relevant registered employee associations); and (c) the employer could reasonably be expected to have known, when he or she made the decision, that one or more of the employees were members of a registered employee association. Notifying relevant registered employee associations" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC may make an order under subsection 532(1) if it is satisfied that: (a) an employer has decided to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological, structural or similar nature, or for reasons including such reasons; and (b) the employer has not complied with subsection (2) (which deals with notifying relevant registered employee associations) or subsection (3) (which deals with consulting relevant registered employee associations); and (c) the employer could reasonably be expected to have known, when he or she made the decision, that one or more of the employees were members of a registered employee association. Notifying relevant registered employee associations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f17785d8708a870a82a1576e2d2e26642f1370259edeaed169dc18c69d3e48c4" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-531 ;
    cof:pageNumber "341"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must notify registered employee associations before dismissing 15 or more employees." ;
