doc:sec-536c-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536C(3) Concurrent operation of State and Territory laws" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does any one or more of the following, in relation to the offence or civil penalty: (a) provides for a penalty that differs from the penalty provided for in this Part; (b) provides for fault elements that differ from the fault elements applicable to the offence created by this Part; (c) provides for defences or exceptions that differ from the defences or exceptions applicable to the offence created by this Part." ;
    cof:pageNumber "348"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536ca a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536CA Dishonesty"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536ca ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, dishonest means: (a) dishonest according to the standards of ordinary people; and (b) known by the defendant to be dishonest according to the standards of ordinary people. (2) In a prosecution for an offence against this Part, the determination of dishonesty is a matter for the trier of fact.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, dishonest means: (a) dishonest according to the standards of ordinary people; and (b) known by the defendant to be dishonest according to the standards of ordinary people. (2) In a prosecution for an offence against this Part, the determination of dishonesty is a matter for the trier of fact.  Chapter 3  Rights and responsibilities of employees, employers, organisations etc."@en ;
