doc:sec-536jj a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536JJ Contravening a collective agreement" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A person must not contravene a term of a collective agreement. Note 1: This section is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1). Note 2: A person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement unless the agreement applies to the person: see section 536JK." ;
    cof:pageNumber "365"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536JK The significance of a collective agreement applying to a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536jk ;
    values:originalText "person (1) A collective agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person. (2) A collective agreement does not give a person an entitlement unless the agreement applies to the person. 536JL  When a collective agreement applies to a person When a collective agreement applies to a regulated worker (1) A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if: (a) the collective agreement covers the regulated worker; and (b) the collective agreement is in operation; and (c) no other provision of this Act provides, or has the effect, that the collective agreement does not apply to the regulated worker.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    skos:definition "person (1) A collective agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person. (2) A collective agreement does not give a person an entitlement unless the agreement applies to the person. 536JL  When a collective agreement applies to a person When a collective agreement applies to a regulated worker (1) A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if: (a) the collective agreement covers the regulated worker; and (b) the collective agreement is in operation; and (c) no other provision of this Act provides, or has the effect, that the collective agreement does not apply to the regulated worker.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "38a81e87e79631e602bf5fbd307ce2fcd382b1670c585ea09032aac778a80531" ;
    cof:pageNumber "365"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.365" .
doc:sec-536jk a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536JK The significance of a collective agreement applying to a" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "person (1) A collective agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person. (2) A collective agreement does not give a person an entitlement unless the agreement applies to the person. 536JL  When a collective agreement applies to a person When a collective agreement applies to a regulated worker (1) A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if: (a) the collective agreement covers the regulated worker; and (b) the collective agreement is in operation; and (c) no other provision of this Act provides, or has the effect, that the collective agreement does not apply to the regulated worker.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    cof:pageNumber "365"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536JK(1) The significance of a collective agreement applying to a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536jk-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A collective agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A collective agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of a collective agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7d8010fb98de93aae43b3079884932b35a9f47ca9e2e6ca91fda5cfaa4a5268e" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk ;
    cof:pageNumber "365"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A collective agreement imposes obligations on a person unless the agreement applies to the person. A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if it covers the worker and is in operation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.365" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1-norm .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1-norm a values:Obligation ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1 ;
