concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536JK(1) The significance of a collective agreement applying to a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536jk-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if: (a) the collective agreement covers the regulated worker; and (b) the collective agreement is in operation; and (c) no other provision of this Act provides, or has the effect, that the collective agreement does not apply to the regulated worker.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if: (a) the collective agreement covers the regulated worker; and (b) the collective agreement is in operation; and (c) no other provision of this Act provides, or has the effect, that the collective agreement does not apply to the regulated worker.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f127602dc4be294398000aecb4cebf1f6d55520f8bb35c8fe06c4a5cd096e53e" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jk ;
    cof:pageNumber "365"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A collective agreement imposes obligations on a person unless the agreement applies to the person. A collective agreement applies to a regulated worker if it covers the worker and is in operation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
