concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jt-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536JT(4) Authorisation of conduct for the purposes of the Competition"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536jt-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Despite subsections (1), (2) and (3), conduct referred to in those subsections is not specified in or specifically authorised by this Act if the conduct is: (a) making a contract or arrangement, or arriving at an understanding, that is or contains a cartel provision that satisfies the purpose condition in either  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Core provisions for this Chapter  Part 3A-1 Exclusion of certain State and Territory laws  Division 3 Section 536JT Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 paragraph 45AD(3)(a) or 45AD(3)(b) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 or the Competition Code within the meaning of that Act; or (b) boycott conduct within the meaning of subsection 87AA(2) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 or the Competition Code within the meaning of that Act; or (c) done in accordance with a term of a collective agreement, to the extent that the term has no effect because of subsection 536MX(1) or (2) of this Act (about matters in respect of which a collective agreement may not be made, or that are primarily of a commercial nature).  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Despite subsections (1), (2) and (3), conduct referred to in those subsections is not specified in or specifically authorised by this Act if the conduct is: (a) making a contract or arrangement, or arriving at an understanding, that is or contains a cartel provision that satisfies the purpose condition in either  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Core provisions for this Chapter  Part 3A-1 Exclusion of certain State and Territory laws  Division 3 Section 536JT Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 paragraph 45AD(3)(a) or 45AD(3)(b) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 or the Competition Code within the meaning of that Act; or (b) boycott conduct within the meaning of subsection 87AA(2) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 or the Competition Code within the meaning of that Act; or (c) done in accordance with a term of a collective agreement, to the extent that the term has no effect because of subsection 536MX(1) or (2) of this Act (about matters in respect of which a collective agreement may not be made, or that are primarily of a commercial nature).  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66f62e6c819f3d46e1a8c0dd4127b1427018a1515f6ae84fb5b3c8a2f15b9d04" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536jt ;
    cof:pageNumber "374"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Conduct is not specified in or specifically authorised by this Act if it satisfies certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
