doc:sec-536kp a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536KP Applications to vary or revoke minimum standards orders" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Any of the following may apply to the FWC for a determination varying or revoking a minimum standards order: (a) an organisation that is entitled to represent, or another body that represents, the industrial interests of one or more regulated workers covered by the minimum standards order or who would be covered by the minimum standards order as proposed to be varied; (b) an organisation that is entitled to represent, or another body that represents, the industrial interests of one or more of the regulated businesses covered by the minimum standards order, or that would be covered by the minimum standards order as proposed to be varied; (c) a regulated business covered by the minimum standards order or that would be covered by the proposed minimum standards order as proposed to be varied; (ca) a national or State council or federation that is effectively representative of a significant number of organisations or bodies mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b); (d) the Minister." ;
    cof:pageNumber "393"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536kq a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536KQ FWC may vary or revoke minimum standards orders if"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536kq ;
    values:originalText "consistent with the minimum standards objective (1) The FWC may make a determination varying or revoking a minimum standards order if the FWC is satisfied that making the determination is consistent with the minimum standards objective. Note: In the case of a road transport minimum standards order, the FWC must also consider the road transport objective.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    skos:definition "consistent with the minimum standards objective (1) The FWC may make a determination varying or revoking a minimum standards order if the FWC is satisfied that making the determination is consistent with the minimum standards objective. Note: In the case of a road transport minimum standards order, the FWC must also consider the road transport objective.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e0efc3ab3919e6fdcd74d07c705731052d7c3fff761ecfb37b68d4a6f5075a34" ;
    cof:pageNumber "393"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "FWC may vary or revoke minimum standards orders if consistent with the minimum standards objective." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.393" ;
