doc:sec-536kt-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536KT(3) Initial matter to be considered for employee-like worker" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the FWC is not satisfied that, on the whole, the persons included (or purportedly included) in the class of employee-like workers to be covered by the minimum standards guidelines, or the guidelines as proposed to be varied, are employee-like workers, the FWC must decide to refuse to consider the application, or not to make or vary the guidelines, as the case requires." ;
    cof:pageNumber "420"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536ku a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536KU Decisions on applications for minimum standards guidelines"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536ku ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an application for minimum standards guidelines is made to the FWC under subsection 536KS(1), the FWC may decide to:  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Minimum standards for regulated workers  Part 3A-2 Minimum standards guidelines  Division 4 Section 536KV Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) refuse to consider the application; or (b) make minimum standards guidelines; or (c) not make minimum standards guidelines; or (d) if the FWC considers it appropriate to do so, instead make a minimum standards order under subsection 536JY(1) instead, as if the application had been an application under subsection 536JZ(1) for a minimum standards order in relation to the regulated workers covered by the application under subsection 536KS(1). (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the FWC may refuse to consider the application if it is not consistent with a direction of the President under subsection 582(4D) (prioritisation)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an application for minimum standards guidelines is made to the FWC under subsection 536KS(1), the FWC may decide to:  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Minimum standards for regulated workers  Part 3A-2 Minimum standards guidelines  Division 4 Section 536KV Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) refuse to consider the application; or (b) make minimum standards guidelines; or (c) not make minimum standards guidelines; or (d) if the FWC considers it appropriate to do so, instead make a minimum standards order under subsection 536JY(1) instead, as if the application had been an application under subsection 536JZ(1) for a minimum standards order in relation to the regulated workers covered by the application under subsection 536KS(1). (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the FWC may refuse to consider the application if it is not consistent with a direction of the President under subsection 582(4D) (prioritisation)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0ce8bacc08f070bd129016c858fa6ca75754a6d4e4d0e365b812fb1e69750b9f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "420"^^xsd:integer ;
