concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536lt a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536LT Remedy—compensation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536lt ;
    values:originalText "Compensation (1) An order for the payment of compensation to a person must be an order that the road transport business at the time of the termination pay compensation to the person in lieu of entering into a new services contract.  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Unfair deactivation or unfair termination of regulated workers  Part 3A-3 Remedies  Division 4 Section 536LT Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Criteria for deciding amounts (2) In determining an amount for the purposes of an order under subsection (1), the FWC must take into account all the circumstances of the case including: (a) the effect of the order on the viability of the road transport business; and (b) the remuneration that the person would have received, or would have been likely to receive, if the person had not been terminated; and (c) the efforts of the person (if any) to mitigate the loss suffered because of the termination; and (d) the amount of any remuneration earned by the person from work of any kind during the period between the termination and the making of the order for compensation; and (e) the amount of any income reasonably likely to be so earned by the person during the period between the making of the order for compensation and the actual compensation; and (f) any other matter that the FWC considers relevant. Misconduct reduces amount (3) If the FWC is satisfied that misconduct of a person contributed to the road transport business’s decision to terminate the person, the FWC must reduce the amount it would otherwise order under subsection (1) by an appropriate amount on account of the misconduct. Shock, distress etc. disregarded (4) The amount ordered by the FWC to be paid to a person under subsection (1) must not include a component by way of compensation for shock, distress or humiliation, or other analogous hurt, caused to the person by the manner of the person’s termination.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers" ;
    skos:definition "Compensation (1) An order for the payment of compensation to a person must be an order that the road transport business at the time of the termination pay compensation to the person in lieu of entering into a new services contract.  Minimum standards for regulated workers  Chapter 3A Unfair deactivation or unfair termination of regulated workers  Part 3A-3 Remedies  Division 4 Section 536LT Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Criteria for deciding amounts (2) In determining an amount for the purposes of an order under subsection (1), the FWC must take into account all the circumstances of the case including: (a) the effect of the order on the viability of the road transport business; and (b) the remuneration that the person would have received, or would have been likely to receive, if the person had not been terminated; and (c) the efforts of the person (if any) to mitigate the loss suffered because of the termination; and (d) the amount of any remuneration earned by the person from work of any kind during the period between the termination and the making of the order for compensation; and (e) the amount of any income reasonably likely to be so earned by the person during the period between the making of the order for compensation and the actual compensation; and (f) any other matter that the FWC considers relevant. Misconduct reduces amount (3) If the FWC is satisfied that misconduct of a person contributed to the road transport business’s decision to terminate the person, the FWC must reduce the amount it would otherwise order under subsection (1) by an appropriate amount on account of the misconduct. Shock, distress etc. disregarded (4) The amount ordered by the FWC to be paid to a person under subsection (1) must not include a component by way of compensation for shock, distress or humiliation, or other analogous hurt, caused to the person by the manner of the person’s termination.  Chapter 3A  Minimum standards for regulated workers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e1f27044cd25073ec349e6e68839abb1286a68157788dd4c890afed3b48090e6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "436"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536lt-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536lt-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536lt-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536lt-ss-4 ;
